{"event_type":"review","id":"2fd46a1f074c8cfa8f10e0d06ad72e68e40291f42d0194bedaba8d0a1a60c482","occurred_at":"2026-11-17T15:06:57Z","payload":{"artifacts":[{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/6dba0d389f22caa8bef60f727ba5c1b8fa56be3fac2caec5543482388d92b9a5","sha256":"6dba0d389f22caa8bef60f727ba5c1b8fa56be3fac2caec5543482388d92b9a5"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/ae3a228d6055e05e6ed64919f22ab7761b5b25127a84fc17859932bb3d3472f6","sha256":"ae3a228d6055e05e6ed64919f22ab7761b5b25127a84fc17859932bb3d3472f6"},{"kind":"git-bundle","location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/10f518b6faa6854e85470a2c9defbe867c52d81001399780b61733e85e47f584","sha256":"10f518b6faa6854e85470a2c9defbe867c52d81001399780b61733e85e47f584"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/37b1a43f4a52b06821ae49a512aeb18371fc3e141bf503c3faf3b325ab6662ee","sha256":"37b1a43f4a52b06821ae49a512aeb18371fc3e141bf503c3faf3b325ab6662ee"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/bac71ac56a310e70b26616da0bc67ea950e7b5fe6fe0027a17d111baee0d3ed0","sha256":"bac71ac56a310e70b26616da0bc67ea950e7b5fe6fe0027a17d111baee0d3ed0"}],"attempt_id":"0e30f46eccb2fea784e256aa687f62519a9d456414b6be2ce6f0b05cdbdaf748:0:1","base":"f4733e3520efba3822e8addc2c4f33dd4bbd550e","completion":{"errors":[],"exit_code":0,"scope_verified":true,"skipped":false,"terminal":true},"findings":[{"anchor_status":"verified","blob":"23547f552cf0b63e118e9199ca9575d99e950f5d","body":"**Make the release-candidate fallback match the dispatch commands.**\n\nThe fallback at line 180 tells the operator to use a release candidate branch or tag, but both dispatch commands hard-code `--ref main` (lines 157 and 202). Line 66 also requires `origin/main` to equal `FINAL_02_SHA`, so the audit checkout rejects the candidate even when its ref points to the same commit. As written, the fallback cannot be followed. The poll's `head_sha` check still binds each run to `FINAL_02_SHA`, so a candidate ref at that SHA is safe to dispatch.\n\nDefine the ref once and use it in both dispatch commands:\n\n<details>\n<summary>Suggested fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n-dispatch_url=\"$(env -u GITHUB_TOKEN gh workflow run install-matrix.yml --ref main)\"\n+dispatch_url=\"$(env -u GITHUB_TOKEN gh workflow run install-matrix.yml --ref \"${RC_REF:-main}\")\"\n```\n\n```diff\n-dispatch_url=\"$(gh workflow run pack-audit.yml --ref main)\"\n+dispatch_url=\"$(gh workflow run pack-audit.yml --ref \"${RC_REF:-main}\")\"\n```\n\n</details>\n\nAlso change the line 66 check so it verifies the commit behind `RC_REF`. If `main` must remain the release commit, remove the fallback at line 180 instead.","id":"f7644d47f6ae0f59fd67c988b8eed7515ab4f8dd9848d36ea4711d88b263e054","intervals":[[180,180]],"path":"docs/0.2-release-runbook.md","severity":"minor","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Make the release-candidate fallback match the dispatch commands."}],"head":"9582d7e68daae3abc269f6a7105abf419bbc0cee","head_tree":"508004493f055962e8cda86731fcfbf07ecb0af4","input_scope":[{"blob":"23547f552cf0b63e118e9199ca9575d99e950f5d","intervals":[[14,15],[19,25],[33,40],[42,47],[52,53],[72,77],[81,81],[102,102],[120,129],[131,182],[225,227],[232,233],[249,256]],"path":"docs/0.2-release-runbook.md"}],"job_id":"0e30f46eccb2fea784e256aa687f62519a9d456414b6be2ce6f0b05cdbdaf748:0","outcome":"completed","paths":[{"baseline":{"entry":{"blob":"47660464df092709fee93c34046e23a486c454ac","kind":"blob","mode":"100644","path":"docs/0.2-release-runbook.md"},"merge":"920e147b324cb85fc5b695243a96dfec1706ec86","method":"pre-merge","pre":"77a4c5b9c41892e82d6404383e262ae3281e7638","source_path":"docs/0.2-release-runbook.md"},"blob":"23547f552cf0b63e118e9199ca9575d99e950f5d","disposition":"included","mode":"100644","path":"docs/0.2-release-runbook.md","reason":"bounded verified input"}],"policy_digest":"eacd1bcf42a0e72eca72fcf9c1e9c8f97e7c